-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter XVI (ss 381-385): FOREIGN CORPORATIONS -- withdrawal,
-- service of process on a corporation that withdrew or never qualified, actions by and against an unqualified
-- foreign corporation, injunctions, and recorder of deeds. Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone
-- (src:1908-1934). (ss 371-380 are in dg10-foreign-qualification.l4.)
--
-- Quote lines are slices of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text): `-- src:N | ...` is line N.
--
-- Subchapter XVI is outside the stockholder-to-member reading of s 114(a) for a nonstock corporation (s 114(b)(3)).
--
-- SEAT: see dg10-foreign-qualification.l4: a director, officer, incorporator or stockholder of the foreign
-- corporation concerned, or its agent, or a person who deals with it or sues it.

§ `Subchapter XVI. Foreign Corporations (continued)`

§§ `s 381 Withdrawal of foreign corporation from State; procedure; service of process on Secretary of State`

-- (a): a foreign corporation that has qualified under s 371 surrenders its authority and withdraws by filing (1) a
-- certificate executed in accordance with s 103 stating that it surrenders its authority and withdraws and stating
-- the address to which the Secretary of State may mail any process, or (2) a certified copy of an order or decree of
-- dissolution together with a certificate executed in accordance with paragraph (a)(1) stating that address.
-- src:1909 | (a) Any foreign corporation which shall have qualified to do business in this State under § 371 of this title, may surrender its authority to do business in this State and may withdraw therefrom by filing with the Secretary of State:
-- src:1910 | (1) A certificate executed in accordance with § 103 of this title, stating that it surrenders its authority to transact business in the state and withdraws therefrom; and stating the address to which the Secretary of State may mail any process against the corporation that may be served upon the Secretary of State, or
-- src:1911 | (2) A copy of an order or decree of dissolution made by any court of competent jurisdiction or other competent authority of the State or other jurisdiction of its incorporation, certified to be a true copy under the hand of the clerk of the court or other official body, and the official seal of the court or official body or clerk thereof, together with a certificate executed in accordance with paragraph (a)(1) of this section, stating the address to which the Secretary of State may mail any process against the corporation that may be served upon the Secretary of State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 381(a) (src:1909-1911)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation has qualified to do business in this State under s 371` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it filed a certificate executed in accordance with s 103 stating that it surrenders its authority and withdraws and stating the address to which the Secretary of State may mail any process` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
      `it filed a copy of an order or decree of dissolution certified to be a true copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it filed with that copy a certificate executed in accordance with s 381(a)(1) stating the address to which the Secretary of State may mail any process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 381(a) the foreign corporation has filed what it needs to surrender its authority to do business and withdraw` `the foreign corporation has qualified to do business in this State under s 371` `it filed a certificate executed in accordance with s 103 stating that it surrenders its authority and withdraws and stating the address to which the Secretary of State may mail any process` `it filed a copy of an order or decree of dissolution certified to be a true copy` `it filed with that copy a certificate executed in accordance with s 381(a)(1) stating the address to which the Secretary of State may mail any process` MEANS
        `the foreign corporation has qualified to do business in this State under s 371`
    AND (    `it filed a certificate executed in accordance with s 103 stating that it surrenders its authority and withdraws and stating the address to which the Secretary of State may mail any process`
         OR  (    `it filed a copy of an order or decree of dissolution certified to be a true copy`
              AND `it filed with that copy a certificate executed in accordance with s 381(a)(1) stating the address to which the Secretary of State may mail any process`))

-- (b): "The Secretary of State shall, upon payment of the fees prescribed in s 391 of this title, issue a sufficient
-- number of certificates ... One of the certificates shall be furnished to the corporation".
-- src:1912 | (b) The Secretary of State shall, upon payment to the Secretary of State of the fees prescribed in § 391 of this title, issue a sufficient number of certificates, under the Secretary of State’s hand and official seal, evidencing the surrender of the authority of the corporation to do business in this State and its withdrawal therefrom. One of the certificates shall be furnished to the corporation withdrawing and surrendering its right to do business in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 381(b) (src:1912)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation has filed what it needs to withdraw under s 381(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign corporation has paid the fees prescribed in s 391` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 391 (piece dg11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 381(b) the Secretary of State must issue the certificates of surrender and furnish one to the corporation` `the foreign corporation has filed what it needs to withdraw under s 381(a)` `the foreign corporation has paid the fees prescribed in s 391` MEANS
    `the foreign corporation has filed what it needs to withdraw under s 381(a)` AND `the foreign corporation has paid the fees prescribed in s 391`

-- (c): "Upon the issuance of the certificates ..., the appointment of the registered agent of the corporation in this
-- State, upon whom process against the corporation may be served, shall be revoked, and the corporation shall be
-- deemed to have consented that service of process in any action, suit or proceeding based upon any cause of action
-- arising in this State, during the time the corporation was authorized to transact business in this State, may
-- thereafter be made by service upon the Secretary of State."
-- src:1913 | Upon the issuance of the certificates by the Secretary of State, the appointment of the registered agent of the corporation in this State, upon whom process against the corporation may be served, shall be revoked, and the corporation shall be deemed to have consented that service of process in any action, suit or proceeding based upon any cause of action arising in this State, during the time the corporation was authorized to transact business in this State, may thereafter be made by service upon the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 381(c) (src:1913)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has issued the certificates evidencing the surrender of the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 381(c) the appointment of the registered agent of the corporation in this State is revoked` `the Secretary of State has issued the certificates evidencing the surrender of the authority` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State has issued the certificates evidencing the surrender of the authority`

-- src:1913 | Upon the issuance of the certificates by the Secretary of State, the appointment of the registered agent of the corporation in this State, upon whom process against the corporation may be served, shall be revoked, and the corporation shall be deemed to have consented that service of process in any action, suit or proceeding based upon any cause of action arising in this State, during the time the corporation was authorized to transact business in this State, may thereafter be made by service upon the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 381(c) (src:1913)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has issued the certificates evidencing the surrender of the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause of action arose in this State during the time the corporation was authorized to transact business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 381(c) service of process may be made upon the Secretary of State in the action, suit or proceeding` `the Secretary of State has issued the certificates evidencing the surrender of the authority` `the cause of action arose in this State during the time the corporation was authorized to transact business in this State` MEANS
        `the Secretary of State has issued the certificates evidencing the surrender of the authority`
    AND `the cause of action arose in this State during the time the corporation was authorized to transact business in this State`

-- "Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only
-- as prescribed by the Secretary of State."
-- src:1913 | Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 381(c) (src:1913)
