§§ `s 382 Service of process on nonqualifying foreign corporations`

-- (a), first route: "Any foreign corporation which shall transact business in this State without having qualified to do
-- business under s 371 ... shall be deemed to have thereby appointed and constituted the Secretary of State ... its
-- agent for the acceptance of legal process in any civil action, suit or proceeding against it in any state or federal
-- court in this State arising or growing out of any business transacted by it within this State."
-- src:1918 | Any foreign corporation which shall transact business in this State without having qualified to do business under § 371 of this title shall be deemed to have thereby appointed and constituted the Secretary of State of this State its agent for the acceptance of legal process in any civil action, suit or proceeding against it in any state or federal court in this State arising or growing out of any business transacted by it within this State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 382(a) (src:1918)
GIVEN `where the corporation was organized` IS A `Where an entity is formed`
      `the corporation has qualified to do business under s 371` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation transacts business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is a civil action, suit or proceeding in a state or federal court in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action arises or grows out of business transacted by the corporation within this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 382(a) the corporation is deemed to have appointed the Secretary of State its agent by transacting business without qualifying` `where the corporation was organized` `the corporation has qualified to do business under s 371` `the corporation transacts business in this State` `the action is a civil action, suit or proceeding in a state or federal court in this State` `the action arises or grows out of business transacted by the corporation within this State` MEANS
        `s 371(a) the corporation is a foreign corporation` `where the corporation was organized`
    AND `the corporation transacts business in this State`
    AND (NOT `the corporation has qualified to do business under s 371`)
    AND `the action is a civil action, suit or proceeding in a state or federal court in this State`
    AND `the action arises or grows out of business transacted by the corporation within this State`

-- (a), second route: "If any foreign corporation consents in writing to be subject to the jurisdiction of any state or
-- federal court in this State for any civil action, suit or proceeding against it arising or growing out of any
-- business or matter, and if the agreement or instrument setting forth such consent does not otherwise provide a
-- manner of service of legal process in any such civil action, suit or proceeding against it, such foreign
-- corporation shall be deemed to have thereby appointed and constituted the Secretary of State ... its agent".
-- src:1918 | If any foreign corporation consents in writing to be subject to the jurisdiction of any state or federal court in this State for any civil action, suit or proceeding against it arising or growing out of any business or matter, and if the agreement or instrument setting forth such consent does not otherwise provide a manner of service of legal process in any such civil action, suit or proceeding against it, such foreign corporation shall be deemed to have thereby appointed and constituted the Secretary of State of this State its agent for the acceptance of legal process in any such civil action, suit or proceeding against it. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 382(a) (src:1918)
GIVEN `where the corporation was organized` IS A `Where an entity is formed`
      `the corporation consented in writing to be subject to the jurisdiction of a state or federal court in this State for a civil action, suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action arises or grows out of the business or matter for which it consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement or instrument setting forth the consent does not otherwise provide a manner of service of legal process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 382(a) the corporation is deemed to have appointed the Secretary of State its agent by consenting in writing to jurisdiction` `where the corporation was organized` `the corporation consented in writing to be subject to the jurisdiction of a state or federal court in this State for a civil action, suit or proceeding` `the action arises or grows out of the business or matter for which it consented` `the agreement or instrument setting forth the consent does not otherwise provide a manner of service of legal process` MEANS
        `s 371(a) the corporation is a foreign corporation` `where the corporation was organized`
    AND `the corporation consented in writing to be subject to the jurisdiction of a state or federal court in this State for a civil action, suit or proceeding`
    AND `the action arises or grows out of the business or matter for which it consented`
    AND `the agreement or instrument setting forth the consent does not otherwise provide a manner of service of legal process`

-- "This section shall not apply to any insurance company doing business in this State." (s 382(b), last sentence.)
-- src:1919 | This section shall not apply to any insurance company doing business in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 382(b) (src:1919)
GIVEN `the corporation is an insurance company doing business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 382(b) this section applies to the corporation` `the corporation is an insurance company doing business in this State` MEANS
    NOT (`the corporation is an insurance company doing business in this State`)

-- The two routes together, with the insurance company outside the section. The two sentences are alternatives
-- ("If any foreign corporation consents ..." starts a new case) and the last sentence of (b) takes the insurance
-- company out of both (fork F35).
-- src:1918 | Any foreign corporation which shall transact business in this State without having qualified to do business under § 371 of this title shall be deemed to have thereby appointed and constituted the Secretary of State of this State its agent for the acceptance of legal process in any civil action, suit or proceeding against it in any state or federal court in this State arising or growing out of any business transacted by it within this State. If any foreign corporation consents in writing to be subject to the jurisdiction of any state or federal court in this State for any civil action, suit or proceeding against it arising or growing out of any business or matter, and if the agreement or instrument setting forth such consent does not otherwise provide a manner of service of legal process in any such civil action, suit or proceeding against it, such foreign corporation shall be deemed to have thereby appointed and constituted the Secretary of State of this State its agent for the acceptance of legal process in any such civil action, suit or proceeding against it. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 382(a) (src:1918)
GIVEN `the deeming by transacting business under s 382(a) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deeming by consent under s 382(a) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 382 applies to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 382(a) the Secretary of State is the foreign corporation's agent for the acceptance of legal process in the action` `the deeming by transacting business under s 382(a) applies` `the deeming by consent under s 382(a) applies` `s 382 applies to the corporation` MEANS
        `s 382 applies to the corporation`
    AND (`the deeming by transacting business under s 382(a) applies` OR `the deeming by consent under s 382(a) applies`)

-- "The transaction of business in this State by such corporation and/or such consent ... without provision for a
-- manner of service of legal process shall be a signification of the agreement of such corporation that any process
-- served upon the Secretary of State when so served shall be of the same legal force and validity as if served upon
-- an authorized officer or agent personally within this State."
-- src:1918 | The transaction of business in this State by such corporation and/or such consent by such corporation to the jurisdiction of any state or federal court in this State without provision for a manner of service of legal process shall be a signification of the agreement of such corporation that any process served upon the Secretary of State when so served shall be of the same legal force and validity as if served upon an authorized officer or agent personally within this State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 382(a) (src:1918)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is the corporation's agent for the acceptance of legal process in the action under s 382(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 382(a) the process served on the Secretary of State has the same legal force and validity as if served on an authorized officer or agent personally within this State` `the Secretary of State is the corporation's agent for the acceptance of legal process in the action under s 382(a)` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State is the corporation's agent for the acceptance of legal process in the action under s 382(a)`

-- src:1918 | Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 382(a) (src:1918)
GIVEN `the process was served by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic transmission was as prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 382(a) the service by electronic transmission is as the subsection allows` `the process was served by electronic transmission` `the electronic transmission was as prescribed by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    (NOT `the process was served by electronic transmission`) OR `the electronic transmission was as prescribed by the Secretary of State`

-- (b): "'the transaction of business' or 'business transacted in this State' ... shall mean the course or practice of
-- carrying on any business activities in this State, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- the solicitation of business or orders in this State."
-- src:1919 | (b) Section 373 of this title shall not apply in determining whether any foreign corporation is transacting business in this State within the meaning of this section; and “the transaction of business” or “business transacted in this State,” by any such foreign corporation, whenever those words are used in this section, shall mean the course or practice of carrying on any business activities in this State, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, the solicitation of business or orders in this State. This section shall not apply to any insurance company doing business in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 382(b) (src:1919)
GIVEN `the corporation carries on business activities in this State, including the solicitation of business or orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 382(b) the corporation transacts business in this State within the meaning of this section` `the corporation carries on business activities in this State, including the solicitation of business or orders` MEANS
    `the corporation carries on business activities in this State, including the solicitation of business or orders`

-- "Section 373 of this title shall not apply in determining whether any foreign corporation is transacting business in
-- this State within the meaning of this section".
-- src:1919 | Section 373 of this title shall not apply in determining whether any foreign corporation is transacting business in this State within the meaning of this section; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 382(b) (src:1919)
